The problem asks us to simulate the process of aliens becoming adults and receiving stones from other adults over $N$ years.
There are $N$ aliens.
Alien $i$ (1-indexed) starts with $A_i$ stones.
Alien $i$ becomes an adult exactly $i$ years later.
When an alien $i$ becomes an adult (at year $i$), every adult who has at least one stone gives exactly one stone to alien $i$.
We need to find the number of stones each alien has after $N$ years.

Let's analyze the process year by year.
At year $i$ (where $1 \le i \le N$), alien $i$ becomes an adult.
Before this event, alien $i$ has been a minor for $i-1$ years.
Wait, the problem says "The i-th alien ... will become an adult exactly i years later".
