At year 2, Alien 2 becomes an adult.
Who are the adults now? Alien 1 became an adult at year 1. So Alien 1 is an adult.
Alien 1 has 5 stones. Since $5 \ge 1$, Alien 1 gives 1 stone to Alien 2.
Alien 2 starts with 0 stones. After receiving 1 stone, Alien 2 has 1 stone.
Alien 1 loses 1 stone, so Alien 1 has $5-1=4$ stones.
So the state becomes (4, 1, 9, 3). This matches the sample.
After 3 years: (3, 0, 11, 3).
At year 3, Alien 3 becomes an adult.
Adults are Alien 1 and Alien 2.
Alien 1 has 4 stones ($4 \ge 1$), gives 1 stone.
