Let $D_i$ be the number of digits of $i$.
Then $f(A) = \sum_{i=1}^N A_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N D_{A_j}}$.

We need to compute $\sum_{P \in S_N} f(P) \pmod{998244353}$.
By linearity of expectation (or just summation), we can swap the sum over permutations and the sum over positions.
$\sum_{P} f(P) = \sum_{P} \sum_{i=1}^N P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N D_{P_j}}$.
$= \sum_{i=1}^N \sum_{P} P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N D_{P_j}}$.

Let's fix the position $i$ in the permutation (1-indexed). We want to sum $P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N D_{P_j}}$ over all permutations $P$.
The term $P_i$ depends on which number is at position $i$.
The term $10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N D_{P_j}}$ depends on the set of numbers placed at positions $i+1, \ldots, N$.
